# Downloads mirror the screen

Applies to every product: Profile IQ, Attribution IQ, Brand Partnership IQ,
Journey IQ, Subscriber IQ, Trends / Rankers IQ, Fin IQ, Microdramas, Ticket
Sales, and anything added later. Product owner's rule (2026-10-29): start bare
bones and strict; loosen only case by case, by name, in the Exceptions list below.

## The rules

1. **Never cross profiles.** A download holds data for the open profile or
   campaign only. Scope server routes by slug/key and re-check access.
2. **Only on-screen fields.** Every column must exist in the table the button
   belongs to, under the same header label and in the same display mode
   (% vs US #, hidden Gen Pop, Data Cuts, Index Source). No URLs, IDs, raw
   values, "Numbers" twins, notes or other fields the table doesn't show.
3. **No bonus or retired data.** Nothing from hidden tabs, hidden or removed
   cards, the tab-shell attic, retired sections, or other platforms/sub-tabs
   than the one showing. No "Read me" or methodology sheets.
4. **Full-length rows are allowed** when the screen can extend the list
   (Top N with a Show all / All option). Rows follow the on-screen sort and
   any active filter or search.
5. **A button exports the table it sits on.** A per-table button exports that
   table only. A "Download all" or "Export to Excel" exports one section or
   sheet per visible table, each following the rules above.
6. **Allowed extras:** the `DATE DOWNLOADED` / `STUDY DATE RANGE` stamp rows,
   and a sheet title line (profile, tab, date, picked audience).

## How to build one

- Prefer building rows with the same functions the table renders with, or read
  the rendered table, instead of re-deriving from the raw payload.
- Do not add a server route that streams a whole source file (S3 object, full
  dataset) to the browser.
- When adding a column to a table, add it to that table's export; when
  removing one, remove it from the export.

## Exempt

- Slide decks (PPTX) and image (PNG) exports.

## Exceptions (approved loosenings)

None yet. Add each approved exception here: product, export, what's allowed,
